Recognise LLVM's libc when deciding whether <stdio.h> has been included.

mini-gmp works out whether FILE is available by testing the include guard
each C library happens to use, and declares mpz_out_str only if one of them
matches. LLVM's libc is not in the list, so the declaration was left out and
src/expr.c called mpz_out_str without one.

This is the same list dev-libs/gmp carries, and needs the same entry.

--- a/lib/mini-gmp.h
+++ b/lib/mini-gmp.h
@@ -299,7 +299,8 @@
   || defined (_ISO_STDIO_ISO_H)       /* Sun C++ */		\
   || defined (__STDIO_LOADED)         /* VMS */			\
   || defined (_STDIO)                 /* HPE NonStop */         \
-  || defined (__DEFINED_FILE)         /* musl */
+  || defined (__DEFINED_FILE)         /* musl */                \
+  || defined (_LLVM_LIBC_STDIO_H)     /* LLVM libc */
 size_t mpz_out_str (FILE *, int, const mpz_t);
 #endif
